From 6cb6695dcb9f24dcd4905348708097142ca273de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 10:54:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 47/76] ipa: libipa: Add a PDAF phase estimator for raw PD
 streams

Many phase detection autofocus sensors, Samsung and OmniVision ones in
particular, do not compute the phase difference on chip: they send the
values of their phase detection (PD) pixels, as a CSI-2 stream of its
own next to the image, and leave the computation to the host. With the
V4L2 metadata series such a stream reaches user space as a line based
metadata buffer, whose layout the sensor documents.

Add PdafLayout, which describes such a stream (the grid of PD blocks,
and which PD pixel of a block each line holds, left or right pupil
half), and PdafPhase, which computes the phase difference in a grid of
regions: the left and right samples of each block row are high-passed
and the displacement that maximises their normalised cross-correlation
over the region is found, to a fraction of a sample. The output is a
phase and a confidence per region, the same shape of data the
Raspberry Pi IPA gets from sensors that compute the phase on chip, so
an autofocus algorithm can use either.

The layout of a given sensor belongs in its camera sensor helper; the
factor from phase to lens movement is a property of the module and
belongs in the tuning file.

The test checks the estimate on synthetic PD buffers with known
displacements. On buffers captured from a Samsung S5KJNS at lens
positions 0 to 700 of 1023 it gives a phase that moves linearly with
the lens position and crosses zero where the image is sharpest.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
